Speed card no longer overlaps boost. Good. But now I notice the ability button at 50px and label "CINDER" overflows to the right edge? "CINDER" text is under the ability, x~314-346, fits. Roll at 290-332, label likely hidden? It's fine.

The top position "6/6" still has "/6" partially behind the lap box? Here the gold "6" at 122-145 and "/6" at ~148-160, lapbox starts 166. Fine, readable.

One issue: joystick and speed card bottom alignment differ (joystick bottom 726, speed bottom 716) — speed is 10px above; intentional.

Now the boost button is quite close to speed (6px) at 360 but no overlap. Fine.

Next, verify the championship final after non-win does not mark completed. Also test champion path via direct API. Let me write a direct test:

- Load page, clear.
- Evaluate: set `Save`? Save is module not exposed. But UI has methods. Use UI:
  - `ui.startChampionship('hatchling')` → this launches race. Wait, it calls launchRace which needs game showRace and assets — fine. Then to process results, we don't need to fly: call `ui.champ` setup manually? We can call `ui.processChampionshipResults({standings:[...first player...]})` three times, incrementing round, then `ui.finalizeChampionship()`.
  - But startChampionship triggers launchRace asynchronously; calling process immediately could conflict. Instead set `ui.champ = {league, round:0, points:{}, playerPoints:0, results:[], finalized:false, lastProcessed:-1}` manually, then call process 3 times with fabricated standings (player first).
  - Then finalize. Check S.leagues.hatchling.completed, unlockedTracks, coins.
- Then verify `Save.leagueUnlocked`? Not exported to window. But check `ui.S.unlockedTracks` includes none for hatchling (no track). For skyward championship: league unlocked after hatchling completed and level >=4 (leagueUnlocked only checks prev.completed and level>=0). Test skyward reward track unlock with champion path, but needs entry 150 coins (we have enough) and set champ manually.

Actually simpler: test hatchling champion sets completed; then check that league card shows "Re-run" and skyward button enabled. A direct query of `#...` after render.

Let me do:
```
await page.evaluate(() => {
  const ui = window.dragonUI;
  const league = ui.champ? null : null;
});
```
LEAGUES not exposed. But champ league can be obtained from existing `ui.startChampionship`? Alternative: use `ui.S` plus find via `ui.renderRaceHub` no. Expose? We can import? Modules not accessible from page. Hmm.

But `ui.startChampionship('hatchling')` sets champ.league. Then immediately override round etc. and call process. But it will launch a race and set view; may involve countdown. We can pause/quit afterwards. Perhaps acceptable.

Actually easier: run through UI 3 rounds but force the player to win by manipulating `game.race` and AI? Hmm.

Simplest: call `ui.startChampionship('hatchling')` (free), then `ui.game.quitRace?` Not needed. Wait 100ms, then set `ui.champ.round=0; ui.champ.points={}; ui.champ.results=[]; ui.champ.lastProcessed=-1;` and call process 3 times, finalize. But game race is starting in the background; the final screen after finalize may be overwritten by race events. We can instead call `ui.quitRace()`? That sets champ=null. Hmm.

Alternative: Grab league via `ui.champ` after calling `ui.startChampionship`, then stop the game (`ui.game.pause(true)`), then process manually. Fine. Results screen not needed; we only test data.

