content.text:
Now replace showHangar, refreshHangarModel, updateHangar with new. Use exact old block lines. Let's craft.

```js
showHangar(dragonId = Save.S().selected, cameraSide = -1) {
  this.clearScene();
  const id = Save.S().dragons[dragonId] ? dragonId : Save.S().selected;
  const d = Save.S().dragons[id];
  const def = DM[id] || DM[Save.S().selected];
  const w = buildDragonSanctuary('hearthfall', this.quality);
  ...
  this.mode='hangar';
  ...
  this.hangarFocus={type:'dragon'};
  this.hangarOrbit={yaw:0.2,pitch:0.22,dist:17};
  this.hangarReact=1;
  this.setHangarDragon(id);
  this.populateHangar();
  this.hangarTarget.set(w.focus.x, w.focus.y+2.5, w.focus.z);
  this.cameraPos.set(... target + offset)
  ...
  this.emit('screen',{name:'hangar'});
}
```
Lighting: warm. `hemi` color #ffeedd ground #3a2c22; sun #ffd8a0 intensity 2.2; add perhaps hemisphere. fog near far.

`setHangarDragon(id)`:
```js
const d=..., def=...
const scale = 1.6;
const m=createDragon(def,{level..., rider:false, castShadow:false});
m.group.scale.setScalar(scale);
m.group.position.set(0,0,0);
this.scene.add(m.group);
this.playerModel=m; this.player=m.group;
const box=new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(m.group);
m.group.position.set(w.focus.x, w.focus.y - box.min.y, w.focus.z);
m.group.rotation.order='YXZ'; m.group.rotation.set(0, Math.PI+0.18,0);
m.group.userData.dragonId=id;
m.update(0.016,{flying:false,grounded:true});
this.hangarPickables.push(m.group);
```
Wait Box3 setFromObject includes group scale and rotation (rotation 0 then). Compute before rotation. Good. But `w.focus` available after build. We need pass focus. `this.world.focus`.
For refresh, preserve focus and orbit:
```js
refreshHangarModel() {
  if (mode!=='hangar'||!playerModel) return;
  const id=Save.S().selected;
  this.disposeDragon(this.playerModel);
  this.setHangarDragon(id);
  this.hangarPickables = [...this.world.pads, this.world.training, this.world.feeding, this.playerModel.group, ...this.hangarAmbient.map(a=>a.group)];
  this.hangarReact=1;
}
```
But `setHangarDragon` removes old from pickables? We can rebuild pickables after.

`populateHangar`:
```js
const owned = Object.entries(Save.S().dragons).filter(([id])=>id!==Save.S().selected);
const bestByFamily = new Map();
owned.forEach(... def.family; score level+bond; keep)
for each [family,d] if world.anchors find anchor; if no skip
const model = createDragon(def,{level,cosmetics,rider:false,castShadow:false});
model.group.scale.setScalar(1.15);
scene.add
box; position set anchor.x, anchor.y - box.min.y, anchor.z; rotation.y=anchor.rotation;
group.userData.dragonId=id;
group.userData.ambient=true;
this.hangarAmbient.push(model);
```
Need avoid duplicate selected also selected central. Good.
Cap 10 (one per family).
Families include hybrid; anchor exists.
If dragon not owned no.

Pickables include pads, training, feeding, model groups.

Camera initial:
```js
const o=this.hangarOrbit;
this.hangarTarget.set(focus.x, focus.y+2.6, focus.z)
const off = this.hangarCameraOffset(o)
this.cameraPos.copy(this.hangarTarget).add(off);
this.cameraTarget.copy(this.hangarTarget);
```
Helper method `hangarCameraOffset(o=this.hangarOrbit)` returns V().set(sin(yaw)*cos(pitch), sin(pitch), cos(yaw)*cos(pitch)).multiplyScalar(dist).

Update:
```js
updateHangar(dt) {
  this.hangarReact = Math.max(0, this.hangarReact - dt*0.9);
  const w=this.world;
  // selected idle
  this.playerModel.update(dt,{flying:false,grounded:true,walk:0.22,excite:this.hangarReact, headTurn: Math.sin(this.elapsed*0.37)});
  // ambient
  this.hangarAmbient.forEach((m,i)=>{m.update(dt,{flying:false,grounded:true,walk:0.1,excite:0,headTurn:Math.sin(this.elapsed*0.4+i)*0.5});});
  // focus target
  let target = ...
  if (focus.type==='habitat') {const anchor=w.anchors.find...; target.set(anchor.position.x, anchor.position.y+2.2, anchor.position.z);}
  else target.set(focus.x, focus.y+2.5, focus.z)
  this.hangarTarget.lerp(target, min(1,dt*4));
  const off=this.hangarCameraOffset();
  const desired=target.clone().add(off);
  this.cameraPos.lerp(desired, min(1,dt*6));
  this.cameraTarget.lerp(target, dt*5)
  this.applyCamera(50,true)
  this.world.update(dt, this.cameraTarget)
}
```
Need avoid allocation per frame? fine.

`focusHabitat(family)` sets target and yaw to view from inner side, dist 20, pitch .25. UI calls when habitat tab clicked? Maybe not, but handle taps.
`focusSanctuary()` reset.
`reactDragon(kind)` sets react and maybe different intensity. Emits? UI already updates. We can create glow burst? Keep simple. For feed, move dragon head toward feed? Not necessary.

`hangarCameraOffset` method.

`handleHangarTap(e)`.

Also add `setHangarDragon` called refresh; it uses `this.world.focus`. If world missing, fallback.

Implement replacing old block.

