Now CSS: fix hint overlap and mobile background. Let me adjust hangar-center hint padding.

Desktop: `.hangar-center { padding-bottom: 14px; }` and stage-hint at bottom. The grid ends at calc(100dvh - 230px)+ top offset. The bottom nav is at bottom. The hint is at bottom of grid, which likely is above nav, but screenshot showed it clipped by nav. Add `padding-bottom: 84px` to hangar-center? That moves hint up by 70px. Actually `.hangar-center` is align-items:flex-end, so padding-bottom pushes the hint up. Set `padding-bottom: 74px`.

Mobile: center height 34vh. If we increase to 40vh and the hint there, still overlap. On mobile, hide the stage hint or put it at bottom of center with small padding. Let's set `.hangar-center .stage-hint { ... }` and in <=900: `.hangar-center { height: 40vh; padding-bottom: 8px; }` and `.hangar-center .stage-hint { font-size: 8.5px; }`.

But the dragon should be visible in 40vh from after header/chips (~210) to 40vh=337 => actually height is 40% of viewport = 338, so region 210-548. Dragon centered on screen (422) fits mostly. Need solid background only after 56% (472). Let's set mobile flex ordering: grid order center=1, side=2, panel=3 already.

Add media query:
```
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .screen[data-view="hangar"] {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(4,13,19,.72) 0%, rgba(4,13,19,.35) 120px, rgba(4,13,19,0) 210px, rgba(4,13,19,0) 44%, rgba(4,13,19,.94) 52%, rgba(4,13,19,.97) 100%);
  }
}
```
Hmm using percentages relative to screen element height (100%). The top padding is 66px. Header 0-150ish. The dragon window ends when side begins. Since grid item center is before side, side starts at header+chips+40vh ≈ 210+338=548 => 65%. So make gradient solid from 62% to 70%. But then dragon from 210-548 is transparent. Good.

Actually the screen element full height 844. 62% = 523. Center ends ~548, close. Set solid at 66%.

But wait the `.hangar-center` height 40vh = 338 and starts after header+chips (~210), so ends 548 (65%). Set solid at 65%.

