Now there's a subtle bug in `refreshHangarModel`: it calls setHangarDragon(Save.S().selected) but does not repopulate ambient, so the previously selected dragon may remain on a pad while a new dragon is on dais; or none. When the selection changes via select-dragon, UI calls `game.showHangar(id)` (full rebuild), not refresh. refresh is called on cosmetics/skill upgrades and after feed? We removed feed render. BuyDragon calls refresh then showHangar(id). So okay. But to be safe, after refresh, repopulate would duplicate because clearScene not called. Better: in refreshHangarModel, remove ambient and repopulate:

```
this.hangarAmbient.forEach(d=>this.disposeDragon(d)); this.hangarAmbient=[];
this.populateHangar();
```
Also update pickables. That keeps everything consistent. Let me update.

