Actually better: threshold 0.025 (2.5%) would capture those nostrils/claws. Let's implement a helper and apply to ambient dragons on medium/low quality. Also I should be careful: the removed meshes are those whose bounding sphere radius * scale < height*0.02. Nostrils (dark spheres) removed, fine.

Wait, that means eyes may also be tiny. Eye meshes are userData.eyeMeshes — important for blinking. Let me not remove eye meshes. I'll skip objects whose material is mats.eye or glow.

Simpler: skip meshes that are in group.userData.eyeMeshes set. Let me implement:

```js
simplifyDragon(model) {
  const ud = model.group.userData;
  const keep = new Set(ud.eyeMeshes || []);
  const box = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(model.group);
  const h = Math.max(0.001, box.max.y - box.min.y);
  const drop = [];
  model.group.traverse(o => {
    if (!o.isMesh || keep.has(o)) return;
    o.geometry.computeBoundingSphere();
    const r = (o.geometry.boundingSphere?.radius || 0) * Math.max(o.scale.x, o.scale.y, o.scale.z);
    if (r > 0 && r < h * 0.022) drop.push(o);
